{title: On the Rock}
{subtitle: Matthew 7:24–25}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Not [Bb]everyone who speaks my [Bb6]name
Will enter in the [Gm]gate of grace
But only those who [Eb]do my will
Find a safe and steady [Bb]place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
A wise man built his house on rock
He heard the words [Gm]and acted true
He did not let [Eb]the voice go by
He made the solid founda[Bb]tion due
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
When rain came down [Eb]and rivers [Bb]rose
And winds beat [F/A]hard a[Gm]gainst the wall
The house stood [F]firm and [Eb]did not fall
[F]Because its base was on the [Bb]rock
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
A foolish man built house on sand
He heard the words but [Gm]did not act
He let the truth go [Eb]out of sight
And built his life on shift[Bb]ing track
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
When rain came down and [Eb]rivers [Bb]rose
And winds beat [F/A]hard a[Gm]gainst the wall
The house stood [F6]firm and [Eb]did not fall
[F]Because its base was on [Bb]the rock
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bbmaj7/A]The [Gm]storm came with [Eb]a heavy blow
[Bb]The foolish house col[F]lapsed and broke
[Gm]It fell with a great [Eb]and loud crash
[F]Upon the sandy, shifting stone
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
When rain came down [Eb]and rivers [Bb]rose
And winds beat hard a[Ebmaj7]gainst the [Bb]wall
The house stood firm and [Eb]did not fall
[F]Because its base was on the [Bb]rock
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Hear the [Bbmaj7/A]words and [Eb]act on [Bb]them
Build your [Bbmaj7/A]life [Gm]on the rock
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
